Imports:
  - Types:
      - Provider
    From: sententia/llm/provider

Usages:
  conventions: .goga/usages/conventions.md
  openai_api: .goga/usages/cooks/openai_api.md
  ollama_api: .goga/usages/cooks/ollama_api.md

Annotations: |
  The OpenaiProvider entity acts as an LLM provider for OpenAI.
  
  Apply `conventions` for coding and testing standards.
  Apply `openai_api` practice when calling the OpenAI API.
  Apply `ollama_api` practice when calling Ollama (same implementation path, no authentication header).

---

"Provider::OpenaiProvider(url: str, model: str, token: str | None = None)":
  location: provider.py
  annotations: |
    LLM provider for OpenAI and Ollama (compatible API).

    `url`: the base URL of the API endpoint.
    `model`: the identifier of the target model.
    `token`: the API key for authentication. When None, the provider skips authentication (Ollama mode).
  methods:
    "generate(prompt: str) -> answer:str": |
      Send a generation request to the OpenAI-compatible chat completions endpoint via HTTP POST to {url}/v1/chat/completions.

      `prompt`: the complete prompt text to submit.
      `answer`: the generated response text returned by the API.

      Implement this method using the `openai_api` practice.
      When the token constructor parameter is None, omit the Authorization header — apply the `ollama_api` practice.

